"The System is run by gods; the Grandfather of Traits (Gramps) oversees traits and souls."
"The Mother of Magic oversees magic and its spells, and hands out quests."
"A third god, called Unc, grants achievements; the three work as an uneasy team."
"Gods feed on mortals' experience, proficiency and deeds; all of it returns to them at death."
"Hostile monsters exist to push people into levelling, feeding the gods."
"The gods dislike anyone interrupting their \"harvests\"."
"Gods sometimes stage world events from boredom, such as a demon king's invasion."
"A god made the demon labyrinth a trial ground and claims all who die in it."
"Quests come from gods; Mother's quests can hide subquests inside like a trojan horse."
"Achievements are an old system thought scrapped; Unc still uses them for his favourite."
"The ways to join the System are to rule a kingdom, control a dungeon, or become a god."
"Dungeon masters and spirits wield powers much like the System's own."
"Rumour holds that lesser gods run the legendary dungeons, the gods' junkyard."
"Gods censor what mortals may say; talk of Earth comes out as \"E4r7h\"."
"The gods can erase a being; one who breaks things was once threatened with it."
"At death a soul earns Reincarnation Points for its deeds, spent to shape its next life."
"One past life earned 5 points: 1 for noble birth, 1 for Prodigy, 3 for Dimension Magic."
"A soul can bribe a god with its earnings to keep its memories into the next life."
"Reincarnators may be reborn only human, elf or dwarf; an elf rebirth costs a great deal."
"Gramps keeps some souls from Earth as [Experiments], reborn as monsters under watch."
"Skills are System-made magic constructs; a skilled mage can rebuild them as raw spells."
"Magic that uses the System's own interface feels eldritch and taboo to its maker."
"A spell projecting the System map fills onlookers with primal dread; they flee it."
